[
 "Rush hour:",
 "forty people",
 "in this carriage",
 "are streaming music",
 "over the same",
 "slice of radio.",
 "So why don't you ever",
 "hear your neighbour's?",
 "You might think",
 "pairing gives",
 "your earbuds",
 "a private channel,",
 "like an invisible wire.",
 "There's no such thing.",
 "Yours share",
 "every channel",
 "with everyone in here.",
 "It's one band,",
 "at two point four gigahertz,",
 "shared with café Wi-Fi",
 "and even microwave ovens.",
 "Classic Bluetooth",
 "slices it into",
 "seventy-nine channels.",
 "And it never",
 "stays on one.",
 "It jumps channel",
 "up to sixteen hundred",
 "times a second.",
 "The jumps look random,",
 "but they follow",
 "a timetable",
 "your phone works out",
 "from its address",
 "and its clock.",
 "Your earbuds",
 "work out the same one,",
 "so they're always listening",
 "in the right place",
 "at the right moment.",
 "Still, someone else's",
 "packet will sometimes",
 "land on your channel.",
 "So every packet",
 "starts with a name tag:",
 "a code made from",
 "your phone's address.",
 "Your earbuds only",
 "open up for that code.",
 "Your neighbour's music",
 "carries a different one.",
 "And sometimes",
 "two packets",
 "hit the same channel",
 "at the same instant.",
 "Bluetooth's own",
 "rulebook calls that",
 "a strong likelihood.",
 "They garble each other.",
 "Your earbuds",
 "don't confirm,",
 "so your phone",
 "sends it again",
 "on the next hop,",
 "milliseconds later.",
 "And a fraction",
 "of a second of music",
 "waits in reserve,",
 "so you don't hear",
 "the gap.",
 "Cafés add",
 "a bigger problem:",
 "Wi-Fi doesn't hop.",
 "A network camps on",
 "about twenty",
 "of those channels.",
 "So your phone",
 "keeps score.",
 "Channels that",
 "keep failing",
 "are dropped from",
 "the timetable,",
 "though it always keeps",
 "at least twenty.",
 "So your earbuds never",
 "had a private line.",
 "They have their own",
 "timetable,",
 "a name tag",
 "and a second chance,",
 "up to sixteen hundred",
 "times a second.",
 "And if you do want",
 "your neighbour's song?",
 "Newer Bluetooth",
 "can share one stream",
 "with any number",
 "of earbuds."
]